📡 8/20 Evening Update: 70,000 isn’t the endpoint—Big Bull is up, and still charging 🚀

This noon, people were still asking, “Can 70,000 hold steady?” The answer is out— not only did it hold, it pushed all the way to $71,626.$BTC  After breaking the 70,000 integer mark, it didn’t dip back. The bulls are truly showing stamina—this isn’t a quick pump-and-run. $ETH  is consolidating around the $2,276 high, taking a short breather.

Why can this move hold up?
🔹 8/21–23 The Jackson Hole central bank symposium is right ahead. The market is pricing in a roughly 80% chance of a September rate cut, and has already bought the “good news” in advance;
🔹 A weaker dollar + institutional inflows + big whales accumulating—solid bottom-buy support;
🔹 The shorts that had been grinding around 65K for over a month were forced to cover after this breakout, flattening them—like adding fuel to the fire.

My take:
🔸 In the short term, strength is confirmed—but above 70K, you’re at historical highs. The higher you go, the bigger the fluctuations. Don’t go all-in chasing when it’s at its hottest;
🔸 If you’re already in, let profits run—while also setting your take-profit/stop-loss levels to lock in part of the gains;
🔸 If you’re not in yet, don’t panic-chase. Tomorrow’s Jackson Hole is the key execution moment—if volume continues to expand, follow the momentum; if it pulls back, wait for a retest to re-enter.

Tomorrow is Jackson Hole. Do you think it will keep charging, or take a breather first? Let’s talk in the comments 👇

